# Architecture Rules

## System Shape

- Monorepo with apps `apps/user`, `apps/trade`, plus shared `core`.
- `apps/user` uses DDD + CQRS + repository layout (`domain`, `commands`, `queries`, `database`).

## Layering (Aligned with `.dependency-cruiser.js`)

- Domain MUST NOT depend on API/controller/DTO layers.
- Domain MUST NOT depend on application handlers/services.
- Domain MUST NOT depend on infrastructure implementations (ports/interfaces are allowed).
- Infrastructure MUST NOT depend on API/controller/DTO layers.
- Commands, queries, and handlers/services MUST NOT import API/controller/DTO layers.

## Data & Persistence

- Postgres access MUST go through repositories backed by `slonik`.
- Write use cases that mutate aggregates MUST use repository `transaction()`.
- Domain events MUST remain coupled to successful persistence via repository base flow.
- No cross-app DB coupling: `apps/user` and `apps/trade` own separate app boundaries.

## Communication

- HTTP endpoints MUST map DTO -> command/query -> bus -> response DTO.
- Message entrypoints MUST use `@MessagePattern` controllers and delegate to CQRS handlers.
- Route/version constants SHOULD stay centralized in app config modules (for example `apps/user/src/configs/app.routes.ts`).
